.TH GENESYS-MCP 1 "2026-08-20" "GenESyS" "GenESyS Manual"
.SH NAME
genesys-mcp \- GenESyS Model Context Protocol server entry point
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genesys-mcp
.RI [ application-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesys-mcp
is the stable public entry point for the GenESyS Model Context Protocol (MCP)
server. It is a small wrapper that execs
.BR /usr/libexec/genesys/genesys-dispatch (8)
with
.BR "--app genesys-mcp" .
The dispatcher selects the validated per-user runtime referenced by
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
and, if it provides a
.I bin/genesys-mcp
executable, replaces itself with it. All arguments given to
.B genesys-mcp
are forwarded unchanged to the selected executable.
.PP
The Debian
.B genesys-common
package does not ship a system fallback MCP executable, because the upstream
MCP implementation is a Python application
.RI ( source/applications/mcp/ )
whose dependencies are outside the Debian build contract. If no per-user
runtime provides MCP, the dispatcher prints a controlled diagnostic and exits
with status 127 instead of failing unpredictably or attempting a network
installation.
.PP
.B genesys-mcp
never performs a network update check.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
Symbolic link selecting the active per-user runtime, if any.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the selected MCP executable, or 127 if no valid runtime
provides MCP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesys-gui (1)
